{"stdout":"docs/design/architecture.md-27-- **Context:** The repo already runs `.ts` sources directly (`node --test tests/` with `.ts` import specifiers and `allowImportingTsExtensions`). The image must be `node:24-alpine`, which strips types natively.
docs/design/architecture.md-28-- **Decision:** The container runs `node src/main.ts`. The Dockerfile copies `package*.json`, `src/` and `scripts/`, runs `npm ci --omit=dev` (which installs nothing, since there are no runtime deps), and sets `EXPOSE 8081`. Compose maps `8081:8081` and adds a healthcheck with `wget -qO- http://localhost:8081/health`, because busybox `wget` ships with alpine. `npm run smoke` is `node scripts/smoke.ts`. New code uses only erasable TS syntax (no enums or parameter properties).
docs/design/architecture.md:29:- **Consequences:** No `dist/`, no `tsc` emit and no extra build stage. `scripts/` is outside `tsconfig.include` and the lint glob (`src`). Both configs are protected, so the smoke script is kept small and plain, and its behaviour is verified by running it (AC-18, AC-19).
